Certainly! Below is the modified sequence of client requests with the `CWD` (Change Working Directory) and `SITE` commands added in appropriate locations:

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
CWD /path/to/directory  # This command changes the working directory to the specified path.
PORT 127,0,0,1,132,209
LIST
MKD test
SITE CHMOD 755 test  # This command might be used to change the permissions of the newly created directory.
QUIT
```

In this example, replace `/path/to/directory` with the actual directory path you intend to change to. The `SITE CHMOD 755 test` command is an example of a `SITE` command that changes permissions for the newly created directory `test`. You can adjust the permissions as needed

